<FlowDocument xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
              Tag="1.0.14" FontFamily="Segoe UI" FontSize="14" PagePadding="24"
              TextAlignment="Left" Foreground="{DynamicResource NightText}"
              Background="{DynamicResource NightBackground}">
    <Paragraph FontSize="26" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}" Margin="0,0,0,6">
        What's New in 1.0.14
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Foreground="{DynamicResource NightMuted}" Margin="0,0,0,20">
        Smoother log loading and inventory updates, plus a usage and error telemetry preference.
        This release history ships with your installed version and works offline.
    </Paragraph>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Keep using the app while history loads
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Choose a log using General &gt; Log file &gt; Browse... or Choose folder....
            Loading history continues to show progress and partial panel results, while tracker
            snapshots run in the background and panel updates give input time to run.
            Log discovery and floating-overlay visibility checks remain active.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Routine inventory checks, tracker maintenance, and periodic saves resume after the
            reader catches up. Closing the app still saves tracking data. Large logs and busy
            panels can still take time to finish; history does not fire alert triggers.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Less waiting after loading
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Inventory export reconciliation now uses indexed item lookups instead of repeatedly
            scanning your saved inventory. Export parsing and tracker save preparation run in
            the background, and queued loot is applied in short batches so it does not all block
            the interface at once.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Run /outputfile inventory in game to refresh owned counts in Inventory &amp; loot quests,
            Ready to merge, and the Mote upgrade planner. Item upgrade variants are still combined
            for ownership counts, with storage locations and loot newer than the export preserved.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Choose whether to share usage and error events
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            General &gt; Application updates now includes Share usage and error telemetry.
            It is enabled by default and sends app starts, fixed feature labels, and error types
            and sources to Azure Application Insights. Untick it to stop collecting new events;
            your choice is saved for future starts.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Game and log contents, character and item names, file paths, exception messages,
            and stack traces are not sent. Azure Monitor may process standard service and
            network metadata. Errors use custom events rather than detailed crash reports.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Paragraph FontSize="26" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}" Margin="0,0,0,6">
        What's New in 1.0.13
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Foreground="{DynamicResource NightMuted}" Margin="0,0,0,20">
        The mote upgrade planner is clearer about equipment copies and has a simpler Spell mode.
        This release history is included with your installed version and works offline.
        Older releases are listed below, newest first.
    </Paragraph>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Spell mode is spell-only
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            In Settings, open General &gt; Overlays and enable Mote upgrade planner.
            Choose Spell and type the spell name. The inventory name list and equipment copy,
            feeding, and farming options are hidden, so equipment choices won't be mixed into spell planning.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Understand copy merges and mote carry-over
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            In Equipment mode, choose Equipment, type a name or pick it from your inventory export,
            then set Current and any Points already invested. Use inventory copies, feeding, and farming
            options apply only to equipment. The extra-copy count and farm rank now stay grouped with
            their labels on a separate row.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            What to do now explains when a copy merge alone completes a rank. If motes are also
            listed for that step, they are used first only when the item is about to outgrow them;
            their points carry into the next rank. For example, a +6 copy alone makes a +6 item
            +7, while eligible motes added before that merge carry forward.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Where to see the plan
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Read What to do for the short instructions and missing motes. In Equipment mode,
            Extra copies to farm and at estimate how many additional copies at that rank are needed
            with the motes and copies selected. Show the math opens the detailed tables.
            Spells use motes only; condensing and Void-Touched motes are not included.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Paragraph FontSize="26" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}" Margin="0,24,0,6">
        What's New in 1.0.12
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Foreground="{DynamicResource NightMuted}" Margin="0,0,0,20">
        Plan upgrades, make alerts easier to notice, and choose a more readable theme.
        This help is included with your installed version and works offline.
    </Paragraph>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Mote upgrade planner
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Work out how to get equipment or a spell from its current +rank to +10.
            In Settings, open General &gt; Overlays and enable Mote upgrade planner.
        </Paragraph>
        <List MarkerStyle="Decimal">
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Choose Equipment or Spell, then type a name or pick an item from your inventory export.
                Picking an item selects your highest copy's rank. Set Current and any Points already invested.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Use owned motes and Use inventory copies count what you already have.
                Your current item is not a spare. Equipment uses the matching mote tier for each step,
                keeping bigger motes for later ranks.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Feed copies with motes first can raise spare copies before you merge them.
                Small motes that your main item has outgrown can still help a lower-rank copy.
                The guide tells you what to feed each copy and in what order to upgrade your item.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Choose Farm at to set the +rank of copies you could collect.
                The guide estimates how many more you need with your selected motes and copies.
                Extra copies lets you try a quantity you expect to get; farmed copies can also be fed with motes.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Read What to do for the short instructions. Still need lists missing motes;
                the farming estimate is an alternative way to finish. Show the math opens the detailed tables.
                A +10 item is already finished, so it has no upgrade steps.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
        </List>
        <Paragraph Foreground="{DynamicResource NightMuted}">
            The Motes overlay also shows equipment and spell values beside each tier.
            Inventory counts come from your latest export; run /outputfile inventory in game to refresh them.
            Copies count as their exact displayed +rank, with no assumed partial progress.
            Condensing and Void-Touched motes are not included in the planner.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Clearer alerts and easier trigger editing
        </Paragraph>
        <List>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                In Settings &gt; Alert triggers, use Simple text for a plain, case-insensitive match,
                Regex for a pattern, or both. Either match can fire the alert; they are OR, not AND.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Trigger cards use multiple rows so the fields are less cramped.
                Choose an alert color with Pick... and select a text effect, such as flash, bounce, or glow.
                Choose None for a still alert.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
            <ListItem><Paragraph>
                Alerts are centered and wrap to fit the panel. Use Test to try a log line and reveal
                the Alerts panel without waiting for the event in game.
            </Paragraph></ListItem>
        </List>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Relearn spawn and spell timers
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            If a patch or an early break has made a learned timer inaccurate, use Relearn on its row
            in Spawn timers or Spell durations. This clears the learned timing so new observations can
            rebuild it. Existing overrides are kept; clear an override if you want to use learned timing again.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Accessibility themes and a more useful preview
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Open Settings &gt; Appearance and choose High Contrast Dark, High Contrast Light,
            Colorblind Safe (Red-Green), or Colorblind Safe (Blue-Yellow).
            Themes now include overlay heading, secondary, and status text colors.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            The preview shows realistic tables, controls, selected and hovered rows, and overlays,
            so you can see how each color will look before Apply &amp; save.
            Custom alert colors and chat channel colors remain separate from the theme.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
    <Section>
        <Paragraph FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="{DynamicResource Pumpkin}">
            Help is now one click away
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Use What's New in the main window's top bar to reopen this page, even with Settings hidden.
            Leave it open beside the app while trying a feature. Close it with the Close button or Escape.
            The README also has new dashboard, floating-overlay, and countdown examples.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            The main dashboard's Always on top checkbox has been removed.
            Floating game overlays still stay on top when they are shown.
        </Paragraph>
    </Section>
</FlowDocument>
